               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>2  Grand marble mausoleum, with stairs leading up to  its entra</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>2  Grand marble mausoleum, with stairs leading up to  its entrance. One of its two large doors is open. On the other, a symbol is messily scrawled in red paint. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>3  Small museum honoring Ardowyn‚Äôs accomplishments. Paintings, </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>3  Small museum honoring Ardowyn‚Äôs accomplishments. Paintings, artifacts, and plaques detail Ardowyn‚Äôs troubled early life,  his inspiring turn toward heroism, and his tragic death from a slowly debilitating arcane curse left by his adversaries before their defeat. At the center of the polished marble floor, an ornate rectangular design cordoned off by velvet rope suggests Ardowyn‚Äôs final resting place. On the far wall, a large tapestry hangs from ceiling to floor, depicting Ardowyn‚Äôs final moment of victory over the Great Adversary and his mightiest demons.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>4  Hidden behind the tapestry, a heavy stone door has been blas</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>4  Hidden behind the tapestry, a heavy stone door has been blasted open. A darkened spiral staircase descends behind it.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>5  Stepping into the crypt, four torches light up one-by- one a</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>5  Stepping into the crypt, four torches light up one-by- one around a large stone casket in the center. A relief of Ardowyn is carved into the top of it. WEapons belonging to the savior hang from left and right walls. two chairs shaped like giant demon hands flank the entrance.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>6  A demon‚Äôs enormous, terrifying head is mounted on the wall o</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>6  A demon‚Äôs enormous, terrifying head is mounted on the wall opposite the entrance. Sharp teeth protrude from its closed mouth, and two great horns extend from its forehead. Its eyes reflect torchlight in an uncannily lifelike manner.   At some point its eyes flash, and a foul stench comes from  its mouth as it asks in a monstrous voice: ‚ÄúWho goes there?‚Äù Unless answered correctly, it bellows, ‚ÄúBegone!‚Äù Flames  lick the back of its teeth before it unleashes its fury. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>7  The defeated or sated demon‚Äôs mouth hangs open, creating a 5</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>7  The defeated or sated demon‚Äôs mouth hangs open, creating a 5x5-foot space to crawl through. Inside smells rancid and feels wet, and a small drain can be found on the floor. A ladder against the wall leads to a gradually upward- slanting tunnel, which ends in a hole overhead. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>8  The hole opens into a fancy bathroom. Next to the hole are f</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>8  The hole opens into a fancy bathroom. Next to the hole are fresh scrape marks on the floor, leading to a free-standing golden toilet a foot away. One portion of the wall, near the claw-footed bathtub, opens up to a bedroom.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>9  Beautifully adorned bedroom and study. Fancy clothes fill a </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>9  Beautifully adorned bedroom and study. Fancy clothes fill a closet to the left. Shelves to the right overflow with books. Writing and painting implements cover several desks, along with piles of scrolls. In one corner is a console with strange mechanical controls and two periscopes, which can spy both down into the lower crypt and up into the mausoleum. To the right is a small kitchen. Across from the bed is a completely glass wall with a glass door in the middle. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>10  Underground garden, unkempt and overgrown. a big tree stand</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>10  Underground garden, unkempt and overgrown. a big tree stands in each corner, stone fountain to the left, and bench to the right. A magical half-sphere glows, sun-like, in the middle. Water drips from the ceiling.   Upon entering the garden, a dark figure may be seen ducking behind the bushes at the rear and sending out several bolts of magic into the room. One hits the sphere, shattering it with a bright flash, then plunging the room into darkness. Other bolts hit the trees, bringing them to life.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>10</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>10</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>10 copy 2</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>10</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>11  Entrance to small tunnel hiding behind overgrown grass, han</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>11  Entrance to small tunnel hiding behind overgrown grass, hanging branches, and untrimmed bushes. The tunnel Leads up at a steep incline, with ladder-like wooden steps. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>11</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>11</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>11 copy 2</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>11</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>12  rough dirt cave. At the far end is a pile of rocks and soil</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>12  rough dirt cave. At the far end is a pile of rocks and soil from a cave-in. On the ceiling above is a flat, stone circle. Toward the front of the circle, a tiny sliver of sunlight can be seen. Against the far wall is a partially- destroyed ladder and a lever near the ceiling.   A shriveled human arm in fancy garments sticks out of the rubble. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>12</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>12</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>12 copy 2</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>12</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Floor trigger  on the first step off stairs cues torches. </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Floor trigger  on the first step off stairs cues torches. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>a large red A is painted on the tapestry. other paintings in th</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>a large red A is painted on the tapestry. other paintings in the mausoleum each have another letter painted on them: d, r, u, and f.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Casket holds an unidentifiable skeleton. </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Casket holds an unidentifiable skeleton. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Boxes and sacks of supplies can provide partial cover in cave.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Boxes and sacks of supplies can provide partial cover in cave.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Purple~ above ground Blue~ Below ground</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Purple~ above ground Blue~ Below ground</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Muri had his engineer change the demon‚Äôs password to a FRaUD. </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Muri had his engineer change the demon‚Äôs password to a FRaUD. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Animatronic demon, made of metal  and animal hide, fueled by oi</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Animatronic demon, made of metal  and animal hide, fueled by oil-based pyrotechnics. Automatically triggered when the head or the weapons on  the walls are touched. too much noise may also alert the visitors in the  next room to operate it manually. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>by Andrew Carl andrewcarlcomics.com  released under CC BY-SA 4.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>by Andrew Carl andrewcarlcomics.com  released under CC BY-SA 4.0 license https://creativecommons.org/ licenses/by-sa/4.0/</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Sources of relevaNt InformaTion  - Flunkies [limited info about</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Sources of relevaNt InformaTion  - Flunkies [limited info about ‚Äúfraud‚Äù] - Engineer Hoku [dirty conscience or here under duress]  - Ardowyn‚Äôs writings [boredom, craving fresh air] - Former Apprentice Muri [vengeful, self-righteous] </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>WhaT haPpened 30 years AGo  SigerafF, self-styled Great Adversa</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>WhaT haPpened 30 years AGo  SigerafF, self-styled Great Adversary of Order, was a famously powerful warlock in contract with even more powerful demons. Muri was his most loyal assistant. They terrorized the realm and undermined its leaders for years. But Sigeraff realized the demons empowering him were more dangerous and hungry for destruction than he‚Äôd originally believed, and his meddling with them threatened all of existence. So, to right his wrong, he planned to seal them away forever with a complex ritual.  Ardowyn was a young conman on the run who stumbled upon Sigeraff‚Äôs lair, interrupting that very ritual. Sigeraff‚Äôs subsequent slip in concentration threatened to let the demons loose. To stop them now, the mage had to sacrifice a life. Choosing among those present ~ Ardowyn, Muri, and himself ~ Sigeraff chose himself. The ritual succeeded, and Sigeraff died.  Seeing a window for redemption ~ and riches ~ Ardowyn dragged the mage‚Äôs head and the severed limb of a greater demon to the nearest city, claiming to have slain them himself, thus stopping a demon invasion. He led local troops back to the mage‚Äôs lair to prove it. Muri fled, fearing for his life and holding a grudge.  Ardowyn basked in the glory of heroism for a while, but when new crises emerged that he was unrealistically expected to solve, he ran out of excuses to avoid them. Believing he was too famous to run away, he feigned a slow-acting curse and built his own tomb  ~ with the help of engineers paid well enough to keep quiet, including hOku ~ in preparation for a fake death. He survived inside for years, living off of his underground garden and offerings left at his monument. He continued to embellish his own legend through writing and art, which he would sneak up to his public mausoleum.  Ardowyn grew to be a symbol of bravery, hope, and redemption, inspiring everyone who heard his name.  An Eventful AnNiveRSary  Over the years, Muri tried in vain to convince the public of  the story‚Äôs true hero, but only turned a few. On the 30th anniversary of Ardowyn‚Äôs deception, he finally found an  inside man to help expose the truth: Hoku.  Meanwhile, the sheer mass of anniversary-inspired donations left for Ardowyn had impeded the mechanism that allowed him out of his secret cave to collect them. When trying to do so several weeks ago, he accidentally triggered a cave-in that trapped and killed him. Buried by his own fame.  Now that Muri has finally arrived to punish and expose Ardowyn, he finds that the ‚Äúslayer of demons‚Äù has already slain himself. What will Muri do? What will the players do?  Will the truth set anyone free? </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>ENCounTerS  [Increase difficulty for higher levels and/or bigge</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>ENCounTerS  [Increase difficulty for higher levels and/or bigger parties]  A  mausoleuM: 2 flunkies. Not magic proficient. Can be fought or reasoned with. Will reveal their boss has gone ahead, and may unwittingly hint at a password. [harder: add flunkies; give them pets]  b  Crypt: Demon Head. attacks twice on turn. breathes fire, bites, flails with horns. Vulnerable to electricity. Immune to mental effects. avoid combat with correct password. [harder: extend fire breath range; 2 giant, clawed hands on opposite wall come to life]  C  bedrOom: 2 strong flunkies and 1 engineer, hokU. If surprised  with successful stealth and/or avoidance of Crypt‚Äôs combat, find flunkies digging through desks/chests and Hoku fiddling with console. Can be fought or reasoned with. [harder: add another strong flunky; add several weaker ones; let one plant a small mimic]  d  GardeN: 1 tree, magically brought to life. Vulnerable to fire. Avoid combat by successfully dodging/escaping branches and entering tunnel. [harder: add some angry shrubs; awaken more trees]  E  CAVe: former Apprentice ~ now BOSS ~ muri. Warlock. Flings rocks from the cave-in as or with attacks, gradually revealing Ardowyn‚Äôs buried body.  Yells about his motivation during combat &amp; Can be appeased. if desperate, may raise Ardowyn as a mindless, undead ally, armed with a brittle, fan-made replica of the hero‚Äôs sword. [harder: add flunkies; oozes congeal from spoiled tributes; summon magic familiars] </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
